@model NexusServiceMarketingSystem.Models.Workflows.AdminReportsViewModel
<h1>System reports</h1><h2>People and catalogue</h2><p>Customers: @Model.Customers (@Model.ActiveCustomers active) · Employees: @Model.Employees · Shops: @Model.RetailShops · Plans: @Model.Plans · Products: @Model.Products (@Model.LowStockProducts low stock) · Vendors: @Model.Vendors</p><h2>Orders</h2><p>Total @Model.Orders · Pending @Model.PendingOrders · Feasible @Model.FeasibleOrders · Not feasible @Model.NotFeasibleOrders · Connected @Model.ConnectedOrders</p><h2>Connections</h2><p>Total @Model.Connections · Active @Model.ActiveConnections · Temporarily inactive @Model.TemporarilyInactiveConnections · Permanently inactive @Model.PermanentlyInactiveConnections</p><h2>Billing</h2><p>Bills @Model.Bills · Billed @Model.TotalBilled.ToString("C") · Paid @Model.TotalPaid.ToString("C") · Outstanding @Model.Outstanding.ToString("C") · Overdue bills @Model.OverdueBills · Payments @Model.Payments</p><h2>Equipment demand (modems and routers)</h2><p>Needed by open internet orders: @Model.EquipmentRequired · In stock: @Model.EquipmentInStock · @if(Model.EquipmentShortfall>0){<strong class="text-danger">Order at least @Model.EquipmentShortfall more units from vendors (Admin &gt; Purchases)</strong>}else{<span class="text-success">Stock covers all open orders</span>}</p><h2>Feedback</h2><p>Responses @Model.FeedbackItems · Average rating @Model.AverageRating.ToString("0.0") / 5</p>
